  "phoneBrandGuideA11yXiaomi": "In system Settings, search for Accessibility. Look for Accessibility → Downloaded apps; some versions place it under Additional settings.",
  "phoneBrandGuideA11yHuawei": "Search Settings for Accessibility, then Installed services or Downloaded services. This guidance covers EMUI and Android-compatible HarmonyOS 4.x or earlier.",
  "phoneBrandGuideA11yHonor": "A common route is Settings → Accessibility features → Accessibility → Downloaded services. Search Settings for Accessibility if labels differ.",
  "phoneBrandGuideA11yColor": "Search Settings for Accessibility. Common parent menus are Additional settings, System settings, or Accessibility & convenience; look under General, More, or Downloaded apps.",
  "phoneBrandGuideA11yVivo": "A common route is Settings → Shortcuts & accessibility → Accessibility. Some versions use More settings; find the downloaded services or apps list.",
  "phoneBrandGuideA11ySamsung": "Open Settings → Accessibility → Installed apps, then select this app’s service.",
  "phoneBrandGuideA11yGeneric": "Open Settings → Accessibility and look for Downloaded apps or Installed services. Use the Settings search for Accessibility if needed.",
  "phoneBrandGuideA11ySelect": "Select the DSH AnyApp service. Earlier versions may display dsh-wish; check the app icon. You do not need TalkBack or the system Accessibility Menu.",
  "phoneBrandGuideA11yConfirm": "Read the system explanation, then turn on and confirm the service yourself. Accessibility can read the current screen and perform taps; you can turn it off here at any time.",
  "phoneBrandGuideA11yVerify": "Return to DSH AnyApp, refresh, and run the screen-reading test. An enabled switch alone does not establish a connected service; check again after a restart or update.",
  "phoneBrandGuideRestrictedWhen": "Use this only if the system reports restricted settings or blocks the service switch. Some installation sources trigger this on Android 13 or later; the menu is not present on every device.",
  "phoneBrandGuideRestrictedInfo": "Long-press the DSH AnyApp icon → App info, or find DSH AnyApp under system Settings → Apps.",
  "phoneBrandGuideRestrictedMenu": "If More → Allow restricted settings is available, read the prompt and complete any identity check requested by the system. If absent, use Settings search or manufacturer help; do not disable system protection.",
  "phoneBrandGuideRestrictedReturn": "Return to Accessibility or Notification access and enable the intended service manually. Allowing restricted settings does not itself grant either permission.",
  "phoneBrandGuideRestrictedOld": "This Android version does not use the restricted-settings flow introduced in Android 13. Return to the permission page and follow the actual system prompt.",
  "phoneBrandGuideOverlayFind": "Search Settings for Floating windows or Display over other apps and select DSH AnyApp. A common parent menu is Apps → Special app access.",
  "phoneBrandGuideOverlayAllow": "Allow display over other apps, then return and test the floating shortcut. Accessibility and overlay access are separate permissions.",
  "phoneBrandGuideBackgroundXiaomi": "Search Settings for Background autostart, commonly under Apps → Background autostart. Enable it only for DSH AnyApp.",
  "phoneBrandGuideBatteryXiaomi": "For ongoing reminders or tasks, find Battery saver in DSH AnyApp’s App info and choose No restrictions if needed. Some versions also offer Other permissions → Display pop-up windows while running in the background.",
  "phoneBrandGuideBackgroundHuawei": "Search Settings for App launch. Select DSH AnyApp, switch from automatic to manual management, and allow auto-launch and background activity as needed. Available switches vary.",
  "phoneBrandGuideBackgroundHonor": "Search Settings for App launch, select DSH AnyApp, switch to manual management and allow background activity. Allow auto-launch if task recovery is needed.",
  "phoneBrandGuideBackgroundColor": "Long-press DSH AnyApp → App info → Battery usage or Battery management. Allow background activity if needed and check Allow auto-launch when available.",
  "phoneBrandGuideBackgroundVivo": "Search Settings for Autostart and Background power consumption management. A common route is Apps → Special app access → Autostart; some versions use iManager.",
  "phoneBrandGuideBackgroundSamsung": "Open Settings → Battery → Background usage limits. Check that DSH AnyApp is not in Deep sleeping apps; add it to Never auto sleeping apps if ongoing tasks require it.",
  "phoneBrandGuideBackgroundGeneric": "Open DSH AnyApp’s App info → Battery or App battery usage. Allow background usage for ongoing tasks and adjust the per-app optimization options shown on your phone.",
  "phoneBrandGuideBackgroundLimits": "Adjust only DSH AnyApp’s needed settings; global battery saving can stay on. The system may still delay reminders or reclaim processes. Test a locked-screen reminder; these settings do not guarantee permanent background running.",
  "phoneBrandGuideAutostartGeneric": "Search Settings for Autostart, Auto-launch, or App launch. If your phone has no such menu, use its per-app battery settings; a missing menu must not be shown as granted.",
  "phoneBrandGuidePopupXiaomi": "Some Xiaomi versions offer App info → Other permissions → Display pop-up windows while running in the background. Adjust it only for returning to a work from the background, if the option exists.",
  "phoneBrandGuidePopupGeneric": "Search Settings for background pop-up windows. Many phones have no separate permission for this. If opening a screen is blocked, return using the task notification or floating shortcut.",
  "phoneBrandGuideNotificationsFind": "Open DSH AnyApp’s App info → Notifications and enable the reminder categories you need. Android 13 or later may also show a notification permission prompt.",
  "phoneBrandGuideNotificationsVerify": "Check sound, lock-screen display and Do Not Disturb settings for the category, then send a test reminder. Notification permission does not grant access to other apps’ notifications.",
  "phoneBrandGuideNotificationAccessFind": "Search Settings for Notification access. This separate permission reads notification content; it is not the switch used to send reminders.",
  "phoneBrandGuideNotificationAccessConfirm": "Select DSH AnyApp, read the system explanation and enable access yourself. Return to select allowed source apps. Only newly received notifications are handled; complete notification history is not guaranteed.",
  "phoneBrandGuideExactFind": "On Android 12 or later, search Settings for Alarms & reminders and allow DSH AnyApp if this option is offered.",
  "phoneBrandGuideExactOld": "This Android version does not require the Alarms & reminders special access introduced in Android 12. Notification and background settings still apply.",
  "phoneBrandGuideExactVerify": "Return, schedule a short reminder and test with the screen locked. Precise alarms, notification categories and background policy must be checked separately.",
  "phoneBrandGuideDeveloperOptional": "This is optional for computer-assisted development. Creating and using works, including accessibility phone control, does not require Developer options, root, or bootloader unlocking.",
  "phoneBrandGuideDeveloperFind": "Find Build number under Settings → About phone / About device, sometimes inside Software information. Tap it about seven times and complete any system verification.",
  "phoneBrandGuideDeveloperXiaomi": "Xiaomi commonly uses the OS / MIUI version in About phone. Tap it about seven times and complete system verification. If Android version opens an Easter egg, go back and find the system version; names vary.",
  "phoneBrandGuideDeveloperReturn": "Search Settings for Developer options and change only what the current development task requires. Debugging can be turned off when finished.",
  "phoneBrandGuideUsbOpen": "In Developer options, enable USB debugging and use a data-capable cable to connect a computer you trust. OEM unlocking is not required.",
  "phoneBrandGuideUsbConfirm": "Keep the phone unlocked and manually approve the computer’s debugging prompt only for a connection you initiated. If missing, check the cable, USB mode and computer driver.",
  "phoneBrandGuideUsbClose": "After development, turn off USB debugging and revoke debugging authorizations for computers you no longer trust.",
  "phoneBrandGuideWirelessOpen": "Some Android 11 or later devices offer Developer options → Wireless debugging. Use a trusted network and the system’s pairing-code or QR flow to connect a computer.",
  "phoneBrandGuideWirelessOld": "This Android version does not support the wireless pairing flow introduced in Android 11. Use USB development instead; the app does not bypass the system restriction.",
  "phoneBrandGuideWirelessNoClient": "This page explains the system entry only; it does not pair automatically or make ADB a dependency for works. Skip if unavailable, and disable wireless debugging and remove unused pairings when finished.",
  "phoneBrandGuideCameraStep": "Grant camera access when a work first takes a photo. If denied, open DSH AnyApp → App info → Permissions → Camera; Allow only while using the app is sufficient.",
  "phoneBrandGuideMicrophoneStep": "Grant microphone access when using voice input. Change it under App info → Permissions → Microphone. A working speech-recognition service is still required on the device.",
  "phoneBrandGuideLocationStep": "For one-time location, allow access while using the app or just once. Use approximate location when sufficient; this feature does not need background location.",
  "phoneBrandGuideCalendarStep": "Only works that directly read or write calendars request calendar access. Change it under App info → Permissions → Calendar. When opening a system event editor instead, you confirm saving in the calendar app.",
  "phoneBrandGuideFilesStep": "Use the system picker to select files or photos to import and a save location for exports. Only selected content is shared; ordinary works do not require All files access.",
  "phoneBrandGuideCaptureStep": "Accessibility screenshots work only where the system and page allow them. If screen-capture consent is needed, the system presents its selection and confirmation each session. Cancelling leaves sharing or manual input available.",
  "phoneBrandGuideCaptureProtected": "Banking, password and protected screens may block reading or capture; permission does not remove those restrictions. This page does not request permanent capture consent.",
